    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 December 1984 ([1989] ATS 21);",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf, p.6",
      "values:originalText": "(f) the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York\non 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4);\n(g) the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities\ndone at New York on 13 December 2006 ([2008] ATS 12).\nNote:\nIn 2011, the text of an international agreement in the Australian Treaty\nSeries was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the\nAustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).\nmember means a member of the Committee.\nrule-maker has the same meaning as in the Legislation Act 2003.\nthe Committee means the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nHuman Rights for the time being constituted under this Act.\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 3\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(2) In the definition of human rights in subsection (1), the reference to\nthe rights and freedoms recognised or declared by an international\ninstrument is to be read as a reference to the rights and freedoms\nrecognised or declared by the instrument as it applies to Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "(f) the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York\non 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4);\n(g) the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities\ndone at New York on 13 December 2006 ([2008] ATS 12).\nNote:\nIn 2011, the text of an international agreement in the Australian Treaty\nSeries was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the\nAustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).\nmember means a member of the Committee.\nrule-maker has the same meaning as in the Legislation Act 2003.\nthe Committee means the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nHuman Rights for the time being constituted under this Act.\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 3\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(2) In the definition of human rights in subsection (1), the reference to\nthe rights and freedoms recognised or declared by an international\ninstrument is to be read as a reference to the rights and freedoms\nrecognised or declared by the instrument as it applies to Australia.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-10-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9214a37150248b80d8c7cba1203b916f3c3a9d5070c444bce8b21706b865fe81",
      "skos:note": "List of international agreements accessible through the Australian Treaties Library."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 December 1984 ([1989] ATS 21);",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 6,
      "values:originalText": "(f) the Convention on the Rights of the Child done at New York\non 20 November 1989 ([1991] ATS 4);\n(g) the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities\ndone at New York on 13 December 2006 ([2008] ATS 12).\nNote:\nIn 2011, the text of an international agreement in the Australian Treaty\nSeries was accessible through the Australian Treaties Library on the\nAustLII website (www.austlii.edu.au).\nmember means a member of the Committee.\nrule-maker has the same meaning as in the Legislation Act 2003.\nthe Committee means the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nHuman Rights for the time being constituted under this Act.\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 3\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(2) In the definition of human rights in subsection (1), the reference to\nthe rights and freedoms recognised or declared by an international\ninstrument is to be read as a reference to the rights and freedoms\nrecognised or declared by the instrument as it applies to Australia."
    },
