    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-4-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Parliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-4-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "As soon as practicable after the commencement of the first session\nof each Parliament, a joint committee of members of the\nParliament, to be known as the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nHuman Rights, is to be appointed according to the practice of the\nParliament.",
      "skos:definition": "As soon as practicable after the commencement of the first session\nof each Parliament, a joint committee of members of the\nParliament, to be known as the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nHuman Rights, is to be appointed according to the practice of the\nParliament.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-4-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d56c5405e27fc5f4d366bbc227c6cb4b8323ae07ef50762870c70e86cccc714",
      "skos:note": "Establishment of Parliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-4-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Parliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "As soon as practicable after the commencement of the first session\nof each Parliament, a joint committee of members of the\nParliament, to be known as the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nHuman Rights, is to be appointed according to the practice of the\nParliament."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-4-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-4-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Membership of the Committee",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Committee is to consist of 12 members:\n(a) 6 members of the Senate appointed by the Senate; and\n(b) 6 members of the House of Representatives appointed by that\nHouse.\n(2) A member of the Parliament is not eligible for appointment as a\nmember of the Committee if he or she is:\n(a) a Minister; or\n(b) the President of the Senate; or\n(c) the Speaker of the House of Representatives; or\n(d) the Deputy-President and Chair of Committees of the Senate;\nor\n(e) the Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives.\n(3) A member ceases to hold office:\n(a) when the House of Representatives expires by effluxion of\ntime or is dissolved; or\n(b) if he or she becomes the holder of an office specified in any\nof the paragraphs of subsection (2); or\n(c) if he or she ceases to be a member of the House of the\nParliament by which he or she was appointed; or\n\n\nParliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights  Part 2\n\nSection 6\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(d) if he or she resigns his or her office as provided by\nsubsection (4) or (5).\n(4) A member appointed by the Senate may resign his or her office by\nwriting signed by him or her and delivered to the President of the\nSenate.\n(5) A member appointed by the House of Representatives may resign\nhis or her office by writing signed by him or her and delivered to\nthe Speaker of that House.\n(6) Either House of the Parliament may appoint one of its members to\nfill a vacancy amongst the members of the Committee appointed\nby that House.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Committee is to consist of 12 members:\n(a) 6 members of the Senate appointed by the Senate; and\n(b) 6 members of the House of Representatives appointed by that\nHouse.\n(2) A member of the Parliament is not eligible for appointment as a\nmember of the Committee if he or she is:\n(a) a Minister; or\n(b) the President of the Senate; or\n(c) the Speaker of the House of Representatives; or\n(d) the Deputy-President and Chair of Committees of the Senate;\nor\n(e) the Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives.\n(3) A member ceases to hold office:\n(a) when the House of Representatives expires by effluxion of\ntime or is dissolved; or\n(b) if he or she becomes the holder of an office specified in any\nof the paragraphs of subsection (2); or\n(c) if he or she ceases to be a member of the House of the\nParliament by which he or she was appointed; or\n\n\nParliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights  Part 2\n\nSection 6\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(d) if he or she resigns his or her office as provided by\nsubsection (4) or (5).\n(4) A member appointed by the Senate may resign his or her office by\nwriting signed by him or her and delivered to the President of the\nSenate.\n(5) A member appointed by the House of Representatives may resign\nhis or her office by writing signed by him or her and delivered to\nthe Speaker of that House.\n(6) Either House of the Parliament may appoint one of its members to\nfill a vacancy amongst the members of the Committee appointed\nby that House.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-5-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "701231ba4a757ebe978ed84637ffb5dd7ebce72fd2164f397d26de8fe3d5b16d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Membership of the Committee",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Committee is to consist of 12 members:\n(a) 6 members of the Senate appointed by the Senate; and\n(b) 6 members of the House of Representatives appointed by that\nHouse.\n(2) A member of the Parliament is not eligible for appointment as a\nmember of the Committee if he or she is:\n(a) a Minister; or\n(b) the President of the Senate; or\n(c) the Speaker of the House of Representatives; or\n(d) the Deputy-President and Chair of Committees of the Senate;\nor\n(e) the Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives.\n(3) A member ceases to hold office:\n(a) when the House of Representatives expires by effluxion of\ntime or is dissolved; or\n(b) if he or she becomes the holder of an office specified in any\nof the paragraphs of subsection (2); or\n(c) if he or she ceases to be a member of the House of the\nParliament by which he or she was appointed; or\n\n\nParliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights  Part 2\n\nSection 6\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(d) if he or she resigns his or her office as provided by\nsubsection (4) or (5).\n(4) A member appointed by the Senate may resign his or her office by\nwriting signed by him or her and delivered to the President of the\nSenate.\n(5) A member appointed by the House of Representatives may resign\nhis or her office by writing signed by him or her and delivered to\nthe Speaker of that House.\n(6) Either House of the Parliament may appoint one of its members to\nfill a vacancy amongst the members of the Committee appointed\nby that House."
    },
