    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Statements of compatibility in relation to certain legislative",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "instruments\n(1) The rule-maker in relation to a legislative instrument to which\nsection 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 applies must\ncause a statement of compatibility to be prepared in respect of that\nlegislative instrument.\nNote:\nThe statement of compatibility must be included in the explanatory\nstatement relating to the legislative instrument (see section 15J of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\n(2) A statement of compatibility must include an assessment of\nwhether the legislative instrument is compatible with human rights.\n\n\nStatements of compatibility  Part 3\n\nSection 9\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(3) A statement of compatibility prepared under subsection (1) is not\nbinding on any court or tribunal.\n(4) A failure to comply with this section in relation to a legislative\ninstrument does not affect the validity, operation or enforcement of\nthe instrument or any other provision of a law of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "instruments\n(1) The rule-maker in relation to a legislative instrument to which\nsection 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 applies must\ncause a statement of compatibility to be prepared in respect of that\nlegislative instrument.\nNote:\nThe statement of compatibility must be included in the explanatory\nstatement relating to the legislative instrument (see section 15J of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\n(2) A statement of compatibility must include an assessment of\nwhether the legislative instrument is compatible with human rights.\n\n\nStatements of compatibility  Part 3\n\nSection 9\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(3) A statement of compatibility prepared under subsection (1) is not\nbinding on any court or tribunal.\n(4) A failure to comply with this section in relation to a legislative\ninstrument does not affect the validity, operation or enforcement of\nthe instrument or any other provision of a law of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-9-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-9-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011-sec-9-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "17603f34a1ce99cae9e306b8ce28a0849046de02c695242352560c451029d93b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-parliamentary-scrutiny-act-2011#sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Statements of compatibility in relation to certain legislative",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "instruments\n(1) The rule-maker in relation to a legislative instrument to which\nsection 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 applies must\ncause a statement of compatibility to be prepared in respect of that\nlegislative instrument.\nNote:\nThe statement of compatibility must be included in the explanatory\nstatement relating to the legislative instrument (see section 15J of the\nLegislation Act 2003).\n(2) A statement of compatibility must include an assessment of\nwhether the legislative instrument is compatible with human rights.\n\n\nStatements of compatibility  Part 3\n\nSection 9\nHuman Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011\nCompilation date: 12/06/2024\nRegistered: 21/06/2024\n(3) A statement of compatibility prepared under subsection (1) is not\nbinding on any court or tribunal.\n(4) A failure to comply with this section in relation to a legislative\ninstrument does not affect the validity, operation or enforcement of\nthe instrument or any other provision of a law of the\nCommonwealth."
    },
